            "\n",
            "KEY ANALYTICAL FINDINGS\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "1. The cleaned dataset contained 392,692 valid transactions from 4,338 customers.\n",
            "2. A temporal cut-off created 3,370 eligible customers with historical purchasing information.\n",
            "3. Of these customers, 1,921 (57.0%) made at least one repeat purchase during the subsequent 90-day period.\n",
            "4. Logistic Regression achieved 66.62% accuracy, 70.65% precision, 70.83% recall, 70.74% F1-score and 73.27% ROC-AUC.\n",
            "5. Gradient Boosting achieved the highest baseline ROC-AUC at 74.64%, showing modestly stronger discrimination than Logistic Regression.\n",
            "6. Five-fold cross-validation showed Logistic Regression had the highest mean ROC-AUC at approximately 74.98%.\n",
            "7. Hyperparameter tuning did not improve held-out generalisation. The tuned Logistic Regression produced extreme repeat-class predictions and lower test ROC-AUC.\n",
            "8. Baseline Logistic Regression was therefore retained as the final interpretable model.\n",
            "9. Frequency emerged as a particularly influential predictor across Logistic Regression and Gradient Boosting.\n",
            "10. Recency, product diversity, spending behaviour and average order value also contributed predictive information.\n",
            "\n",
            "BUSINESS INTERPRETATION\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "Customers with stronger historical purchasing activity showed a greater likelihood of purchasing again within the 90-day prediction period.\n",
            "Purchase frequency was especially informative, suggesting that retailers could prioritise customers with established repeat transaction patterns when designing retention campaigns.\n",
            "Recency also provided meaningful predictive information, indicating that the timing of previous purchases can support customer targeting decisions.\n",
            "The results also show that more complex machine-learning models do not automatically provide superior or more stable predictive performance.\n",
            "The final Logistic Regression model offers a practical balance between predictive discrimination and managerial interpretability.\n",
            "\n",
            "KEY LIMITATIONS\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "- The analysis uses historical transactions from one online retail dataset.\n",
            "- Results may not generalise directly to other retailers, markets or time periods.\n",
            "- Predictive associations should not be interpreted as causal relationships.\n",
            "- The 90-day prediction horizon represents one specific operational definition of repeat purchasing.\n",
            "- Customer demographic and marketing-interaction variables were unavailable.\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "ANALYSIS COMPLETE — ALL CORE DATA PREPARATION, MODELLING, VALIDATION, DIAGNOSTIC AND INTERPRETATION STAGES HAVE BEEN COMPLETED.\n",
            "===========================================================================\n"
          ]
